==Russian==

===Etymology===
{{borrowing|fr|abat-jour|lang=ru}}, from {{term|abattre|lang=fr}} (see {{term|bēatan|lang=ang}}) + {{term|jour|lang=fr}} (see [[журнал]]). 

Cognate with {{etyl|cs|-}} {{term|abažúr|lang=cs}} and {{etyl|pl|-}} {{term|abażur|lang=pl}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|/ɐ.bɐˈʐur/|lang=ru}}
* {{audio|Ru-абажур.ogg|audio}}

===Noun===
{{ru-noun|абажу́р|m-in}}

# [[lampshade]]
# {{context|dated|lang=ru}} a [[visor]], worn on the forehead to protect one's [[eye|eyes]] from the [[sun]]
# {{context|slang|lang=ru}} [[head]]
# {{context|slang|humorous|lang=ru}} [[order]], [[norm]] {{gloss|pun on {{term|ажур|lang=ru}}}}
#: {{usex|[[всё|Всё]] [[в]] '''абажу́ре'''|t=Everything's in order|lang=ru}}

====Declension====
{{ru-noun-1|абажу́р}}

====Synonyms====
* {{sense|lampshade}} [[покрышка#Russian|покры́шка]], [[колпак#Russian|колпа́к]], [[плафон#Russian|плафо́н]]
* {{sense|visor}} [[козырёк#Russian|козырёк]]
* {{sense|head}} [[голова#Russian|голова́]], [[башка#Russian|башка́]]
* {{sense|order, norm}} [[ажур#Russian|ажу́р]], [[порядок#Russian|поря́док]]

